First Author: Choshi
Title: Long short-term memory algorithm for personalized tacrolimus dosing: A simple and effective time series forecasting approach post-lung transplantation
Source number: 9  ￼

Very short summary: This single-center retrospective study developed an LSTM-based time-series tool to predict tacrolimus trough levels (TTLs) after lung transplantation. Five key findings were: (1) the development dataset included 117 lung transplant recipients with 87,112 clinical data points and 3,327 measured TTL time points; (2) SHAP showed that prior tacrolimus dose and prior TTL were by far the most influential predictors of the next TTL; (3) the simplest LSTM model using only tacrolimus-related factors—previous TTL, dose, and route—performed best; (4) the final model predicted TTLs within 30% of the true value at 88.5% of time points and had test-set R² of 0.67; and (5) in 6 subsequent simulation cases, the tool rapidly approached actual TTLs and identified situations where dose increase or decrease would likely have improved control. Figures 1-7 and Table 1 were directly used for extraction.  ￼

